WEBVTT

00:00:00.583 --> 00:00:13.583
Another tool that's very handy when you're working with a coated breed dog is scissors.

00:00:12.625 --> 00:00:16.333
Lot of different types of scissors.

00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:19.416
I'm going to show you 2 types.

00:00:18.666 --> 00:00:24.375
This is just your straight regular scissors.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.416
It's actually a straight blade.

00:00:26.458 --> 00:00:31.958
It's a relatively straight blade in this type of scissor.

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:38.916
Depending on what you're comfortable working with, you can get longer bladed scissors.

00:00:37.958 --> 00:00:49.375
You want to make sure that when you're picking out your scissors you try a bunch of different pair and make sure that the action is comfortable and smooth.

00:00:51.708 --> 00:00:54.000
This a nice pair of scissors.

00:00:53.125 --> 00:00:56.625
These scissors are probably 30 years old.

00:00:55.666 --> 00:01:01.625
Make sure that the scissors are balanced and comfortable in your hand.

00:01:00.916 --> 00:01:12.833
These scissors can be used for trimming around the eyes, trimming around the face, trimming around the feet.

00:01:11.958 --> 00:01:18.166
It's important that you've got a comfortable pair that's manageable in your hand.

00:01:17.208 --> 00:01:20.583
They do make left handed scissors.

00:01:19.666 --> 00:01:24.250
Again, I'm left handed, but I've learned to do everything with right hand.

00:01:23.291 --> 00:01:31.916
For those of you who are left handed and really need to be left handed, they do make left handed scissors and so you can find them.

00:01:31.041 --> 00:01:38.125
Another pair of scissors we've got here are the thinning shears.

00:01:37.375 --> 00:01:41.958
Again, you want to get a pair that is comfortable in your hand.

00:01:41.125 --> 00:01:43.416
There's many different types.

00:01:42.875 --> 00:01:58.333
This type of thinning shear has the tines cut into the blade on one side and the other side as you can see, is just the blade; it's flat.

00:01:57.375 --> 00:02:01.166
You can use on different parts of the dog.

00:02:00.208 --> 00:02:03.208
Again, when you're working around the face, working on the feet.

00:02:02.416 --> 00:02:11.125
You would really have no reason to cut the body hair, but if you are not showing your dog and you do want to trim up some of it then this would give you a more natural look than if you just used the straight shears, which would just cut a blunt end.

00:02:10.166 --> 00:02:11.416
Most dog breeds when you're showing them should not be scissored.

00:02:10.458 --> 00:02:11.708
It happens, but they shouldn't be.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.250
If you've got a dog at home and you just want to trim some of the coat off, then scissors can be very handy to use.

00:02:11.291 --> 00:02:12.958
Important when you're getting scissors, make sure they're comfortable in your hands, that the blade is a good quality and you can get them sharpened.

00:02:12.083 --> 00:02:13.375
Depending on how much you use them, you ought to get them sharpened about once a year.

00:02:12.416 --> 00:02:14.083
You don't want to be pulling or breaking the dog's coat when you're using them on the coat.
